(5471982, 787897, 60173, '<td valign="top">Ouch... This is a fine image that would have scored pretty well, but your calibration is way off. Your background is dark grey, and the image as a whole has a grey haze.</td>', 'Ouch... This is a fine image that would have scored pretty well, but your calibration is way off. Your background is dark grey, and the image as a whole has a grey haze.', '2009-05-06 07:05:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5471987, 788522, 67152, '<td valign="top">lovely light - well captured intimate portrait - it separates itself from the great majority of other portraits in the challenge with a realistic feel</td>', 'lovely light - well captured intimate portrait - it separates itself from the great majority of other portraits in the challenge with a realistic feel', '2009-05-06 07:07:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5471989, 788665, 60173, '<td valign="top">I think this image could have a much stronger presence as a square crop with about an inch cropped off the bottom and about a half inch cropped off the top.</td>', 'I think this image could have a much stronger presence as a square crop with about an inch cropped off the bottom and about a half inch cropped off the top.', '2009-05-06 07:08:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5471991, 788701, 67152, '<td valign="top">I will be honest here....Clearly this shot shows some darkness but i don''t see a specific subject to really hold interest.   The shot appears to have been fired into the neighborhood from a front porch of a house with the flash on creating a very snapshot feel.  Placing the camera on a tripod or other steady surface, turning off the flash, and setting the camera on a timer would allow for a much less ''snapshot'' feel.</td>', 'I will be honest here....Clearly this shot shows some darkness but i don''t see a specific subject to really hold interest.   The shot appears to have been fired into the neighborhood from a front porch of a house with the flash on creating a very snapshot feel.  Placing the camera on a tripod or other steady surface, turning off the flash, and setting the camera on a timer would allow for a much less ''snapshot'' feel.', '2009-05-06 07:10:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5471995, 788273, 67152, '<td valign="top">the concept of shooting the path at night really works for me, but the fact that the image is fuzzy and that the horizon appears to be askew really takes away from the image.  I think a better perspective to draw the viewer in would be to leverage the path to pull our eyes into the scene</td>', 'the concept of shooting the path at night really works for me, but the fact that the image is fuzzy and that the horizon appears to be askew really takes away from the image.  I think a better perspective to draw the viewer in would be to leverage the path to pull our eyes into the scene', '2009-05-06 07:13:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5471999, 788714, 60173, '<td valign="top">This takes me back to basic art class when the teacher would try to explain tones, and would have us draw a black and white image with charcoal. We all failed miserably, but you have clearly succeeded here. I love it.<br/> <br/>=)</td>', 'This takes me back to basic art class when the teacher would try to explain tones, and would have us draw a black and white image with charcoal. We all failed miserably, but you have clearly succeeded here. I love it. =)', '2009-05-06 07:17:08.000000', NULL, 1),
