(5473166, 788458, 100393, '<td valign="top">Amazing shot - I am sure this will ribbon, probably blue!</td>', 'Amazing shot - I am sure this will ribbon, probably blue!', '2009-05-06 17:18:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473176, 788537, 101256, '<td valign="top">Very clever and inventive - the eyes, nose, mouth apparent in the thumbnail sort of resolved into eyes/mouth on full view, but a very good concept captured perfectly. A little less flash would have helped as the center of the image around the door seems a little overdone, but that''s a very minor nit pick. Well done.</td>', 'Very clever and inventive - the eyes, nose, mouth apparent in the thumbnail sort of resolved into eyes/mouth on full view, but a very good concept captured perfectly. A little less flash would have helped as the center of the image around the door seems a little overdone, but that''s a very minor nit pick. Well done.', '2009-05-06 17:22:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473183, 787838, 101256, '<td valign="top">There is a very effective monotone feel to this even though it''s not a monotone image. Very dramatic in feel and dark and forebidding from an emotional standpoint - a very good artistic success. From a technical standpoint, it''s a little oversharpened, but that can be viewed two ways - as a positive halo effect or a negative one. Given the rich and variable detail, the positive approach is much more valid. Well done.</td>', 'There is a very effective monotone feel to this even though it''s not a monotone image. Very dramatic in feel and dark and forebidding from an emotional standpoint - a very good artistic success. From a technical standpoint, it''s a little oversharpened, but that can be viewed two ways - as a positive halo effect or a negative one. Given the rich and variable detail, the positive approach is much more valid. Well done.', '2009-05-06 17:25:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473217, 788500, 101256, '<td valign="top">Often when reviewing these images, it''s a real strong temptation to look at it from a personal POV and say "well, this is what I would have done". In this case, it''s really strong as in this reviewer''s opinion, it would have been much more effective if the door were closed and the lighting was allowed to work against the dark by it''self. That being said, this does work very well and it''s a creative look at the typical horror movie genre reveal shot. The white is right on the edge and the dark shadows and shadowed model impart a sense of surprize and curiosit - again, a typical genre shot. While the image appears to be grainy, it only enhances the artistic feel to this image. Well done.</td>', 'Often when reviewing these images, it''s a real strong temptation to look at it from a personal POV and say "well, this is what I would have done". In this case, it''s really strong as in this reviewer''s opinion, it would have been much more effective if the door were closed and the lighting was allowed to work against the dark by it''self. That being said, this does work very well and it''s a creative look at the typical horror movie genre reveal shot. The white is right on the edge and the dark shadows and shadowed model impart a sense of surprize and curiosit - again, a typical genre shot. While the image appears to be grainy, it only enhances the artistic feel to this image. Well done.', '2009-05-06 17:38:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473288, 787660, 53548, '<td valign="top">striking photo. 10</td>', 'striking photo. 10', '2009-05-06 18:14:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473289, 788294, 53548, '<td valign="top">what the hell... i see this horse in the middle of this. makes it a 10</td>', 'what the hell... i see this horse in the middle of this. makes it a 10', '2009-05-06 18:16:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473469, 788748, 101256, '<td valign="top">Excellant DOF control with the vague, yet detailed background. The image appears to be slightly over sharpened with the "sawtooth" effect in several places around the image which is a very minor issue as it''s not readily apparent on first view. The grain enhances the artistic presence of this image and the total effect is very positive imparting a lot of artistic impact - almost like the accretion disc of a black hole. Very scifi. Well done.</td>', 'Excellant DOF control with the vague, yet detailed background. The image appears to be slightly over sharpened with the "sawtooth" effect in several places around the image which is a very minor issue as it''s not readily apparent on first view. The grain enhances the artistic presence of this image and the total effect is very positive imparting a lot of artistic impact - almost like the accretion disc of a black hole. Very scifi. Well done.', '2009-05-06 19:55:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473517, 787830, 101256, '<td valign="top">Incredibly effective - very Hitchcockian which could very easily been a cut scene from any of his movies. Very effective and very noir. The lighting angle with the rich dramatic black and abrupt facial shadows give a feeling of intensity not often seen in images like that. Simply outstanding from both a technical and artistic standpoint. One more comment - this image would have worked framed smaller with the dark cut off right at the ear. While the partially lighted ear gives the scene some depth and dimension and transitions the light angle from the face to the wall, it just seems a little out of place. A crop just to the right edge would have helped and a total clone out would provide a two step technique to the lighting which might improve it very slightly. That being said, this is perfect as it is and the ear comment was only something to experiment with. This would work really well as an entry into a print competition. Well done - congratulations. By rights a ribbon winner hands down.</td>', 'Incredibly effective - very Hitchcockian which could very easily been a cut scene from any of his movies. Very effective and very noir. The lighting angle with the rich dramatic black and abrupt facial shadows give a feeling of intensity not often seen in images like that. Simply outstanding from both a technical and artistic standpoint. One more comment - this image would have worked framed smaller with the dark cut off right at the ear. While the partially lighted ear gives the scene some depth and dimension and transitions the light angle from the face to the wall, it just seems a little out of place. A crop just to the right edge would have helped and a total clone out would provide a two step technique to the lighting which might improve it very slightly. That being said, this is perfect as it is and the ear comment was only something to experiment with. This would work really well as an entry into a print competition. Well done - congratulations. By rights a ribbon winner hands down.', '2009-05-06 20:27:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473528, 788552, 101256, '<td valign="top">Very inventive and unique so far in this challenge. Creativity is always a highly prized component in any competitive endeavor and this demonstrates that axiom. Simple and elegant, the image is technically perfect and artistically impressive. While up against some stiff competition, it should place very high if not win a ribbon just for originality in addition to it''s technical and artistic success. Well done.</td>', 'Very inventive and unique so far in this challenge. Creativity is always a highly prized component in any competitive endeavor and this demonstrates that axiom. Simple and elegant, the image is technically perfect and artistically impressive. While up against some stiff competition, it should place very high if not win a ribbon just for originality in addition to it''s technical and artistic success. Well done.', '2009-05-06 20:30:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473549, 787660, 101256, '<td valign="top">The silhouette technique used here is intriguing and effective - a common color technique translated into black and white. All the common elements that make up a black and white image are present and effective. There is a technical issue with the lower corners fading which is a negative as, while not a distraction exactly, it doesn''t have a matching face at the top of the image and seems out of place. Still, a very worthy entry into the challenge with detail and inventive use of the silhouette techniqe.</td>', 'The silhouette technique used here is intriguing and effective - a common color technique translated into black and white. All the common elements that make up a black and white image are present and effective. There is a technical issue with the lower corners fading which is a negative as, while not a distraction exactly, it doesn''t have a matching face at the top of the image and seems out of place. Still, a very worthy entry into the challenge with detail and inventive use of the silhouette techniqe.', '2009-05-06 20:41:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5473558, 788458, 100687, '<td valign="top">This is really beautiful. What distracts me about this photo is that her nose is too soft, when it should''nt be. I think this will ribbon!</td>', 'This is really beautiful. What distracts me about this photo is that her nose is too soft, when it should''nt be. I think this will ribbon!', '2009-05-06 20:48:27.000000', NULL, 1),
